    "text": "To determine how much the convenience store pays for syrup a week, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the number of syrup boxes needed per week:**\n   The convenience store sells 180 gallons of soda a week. Each syrup box can make 30 gallons of soda.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Number of syrup boxes needed} = \\frac{\\text{Total gallons of soda sold per week}}{\\text{Gallons of soda per syrup box}} = \\frac{180}{30} = 6\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the total cost of the syrup boxes:**\n   Each syrup box costs $40. The store needs 6 syrup boxes.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total cost} = \\text{Number of syrup boxes} \\times \\text{Cost per syrup box} = 6 \\times 40 = 240\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the convenience store pays \\(\\boxed{240}\\) dollars for syrup a week.",
